dialogue onn
  node root onn "Mind the step. It's wet, and I've swept it twice."
    > "You knew the Arcadia's crew?" -> crew
    > "What's wrong with the Straits?" -> straits
    > "Do you need help with anything?" -> help
    > "I'll leave you to it." -> bye
  node crew onn "My husband's cousin. And the boy from the end house, and the two brothers who kept the chandlery before the chandler. Ten off this street, and twelve more from down the hill. I counted them out and I counted them back, and only the first part worked."
    > "What happened to them?" -> straits
  node straits onn "There's a place past the reef where the water goes quiet. Not calm — quiet. The fishermen won't say the name of it. They call it the Lull."
    > "You believe that?" -> believe
    > "The Lull." -> lull
  node lull onn "Don't say it twice, and don't say it while you're out there. If you go into the Lull and something calls your name, you don't answer. You understand me? You don't answer."
    > "I understand." -> promise
  node believe onn "I believe twenty-two people went out and didn't come back, and the men who own the ships would rather it was weather. Belief is what's left when the paperwork runs out."
    > "That's fair." -> promise
  node help onn "No, child. I've the broom and the step and a great deal of time. What I'd like is for one person to come back and tell me what's out there."
    > "I'll try." -> promise
  node promise onn "Then try. And clerk — when the paperwork's done, come and tell me. Not the harbourmaster. Me."
    > "I will." -> bye
  node bye onn "Step. Wet. Mind it."
  # Act IV: the Marrow home, and the clerk come to tell her.
  node home onn "The clerk. You've the face of somebody at the end of something. Go on, then."
    > "You asked me to come and tell you. Not the harbourmaster. You." if seen:onn.promise -> salt
    > "They're home, Onn. All hands." if not seen:onn.promise -> salt
  node salt fenn "All hands. They were on Gullet Key, raking salt for Silas Cray. Three years."
    -> swept
  node swept onn "Salt. Three years I swept this step for drowned men, and they were raking salt."
    > "And the Lull: something did call the Marrow's name in the fog. Through a speaking-trumpet. Nobody answered." if seen:onn.lull -> trumpet
    > "Not a drop of it was weather." -> count
  node trumpet onn "A trumpet. (She laughs, once, like a door nobody's opened in years.) Three years the fishermen have been frightened of a man with a trumpet and a form."
    -> count
  node count onn "Ten off this street. I'll count them back now; I said I would. (She leans the broom against the door.) Mind the step, clerk. It's wet, and I'm not sweeping it again tonight."
